the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    *a person* is a person.
    *a person* is *a number* years of age.

the knowledge base logical_constraints includes:

the text of the Logical Constraints is at "sources/logical_constraints.md".

the text of the Blawx project is at "sources/logical_constraints.yaml".

% The Act, section by section.
bob is a person, as stated in the Logical Constraints at section 1.

bob is 40 years of age, as stated in the Logical Constraints at section 2.

bob is 50 years of age, as stated in the Logical Constraints at section 4.

% The constraint of section 3 of the Logical Constraints: no case may meet these conditions — one that does is inconsistent, and nothing follows from it.
it must not be true that
    a person is a person
    and the person is a number years of age
    and the person is a second number years of age
    and the number is not equal to the second number.

scenario how_old_bob is, as stated in the Blawx project at test how_old_bob:
    % This query returns no models, because the constraint in section
    % 3 has been violated, which renders the entire model inconsistent.
    % If you disable section 4, this query will answer "40".
    % If you disabled section 3, it will answer "40 and 50".
    how_old_bob expects answers [].

query how_old_bob is:
    bob is which number years of age.

the view the act is:
    the title is "Logical Constraints, as Blawx encodes it".
    the case is a scenario, with the documents it is stated in.
    the result is the answer to query how_old_bob.
    the result shows its reasons.
    the result shows its citations.
    the result can be flipped.

